THIRD-PARTY DATA
================

No third-party dataset is redistributed in this repository.  Every external source
below is downloaded at run time by the scripts named in `README.md` into `data/`,
which is not versioned.  The attributions required by each source are reproduced
here and in `README.md`.

1. Challenge data (12 monthly training files, `ranking.parquet`,
   `submitting.parquet`)
   EUROCONTROL Performance Review Commission and the OpenSky Network,
   PRC Data Challenge 2026.  Distributed by the organisers through a per-team
   MinIO bucket and NOT redistributed here.
   <https://ansperformance.eu/study/data-challenge/dc2026/>

2. ADS-B / MLAT traces — adsb.lol global history
   `globe_history_2025`, `globe_history_2026`.
   Licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0.
   Contains information from adsb.lol, which is made available under the ODbL
   <https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/>.
   <https://adsb.lol/> · <https://github.com/adsblol/globe_history_2025>

3. Daily ATFM and pre-departure delay series — EUROCONTROL
   `atfm_slot_adherence`, `all_pre_departure_delays`, `atc_pre_departure_delays`.
   Public EUROCONTROL performance data, free to use with attribution.
   Source: EUROCONTROL Performance Review Unit, <https://ansperformance.eu/csv/>

4. OPDI v0.0.2 flight lists — Open Performance Data Initiative
   (EUROCONTROL / OpenSky Network).  Open data: "can be freely used, reused and
   distributed provided that the data source is attributed".
   Source: Open Performance Data Initiative, <https://www.opdi.aero/>

5. METAR surface observations — Iowa Environmental Mesonet (IEM) ASOS/AWOS/METAR
   archive, Iowa State University, built on NOAA data.  Public data, free to use
   with attribution.
   <https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/request/download.phtml>

6. Airport geometry — X-Plane `apt.dat` from the X-Plane Airport Scenery Gateway.
   The apt.dat airport data is released by the X-Plane Scenery Gateway
   contributors under the GNU General Public License.  The official file-format
   specification states:

       "The GNU GPL (General Public License) under which this data is released
        requires that the copyright notice be maintained with the data."

   Accordingly: X-Plane airport data (`apt.dat`), Copyright (C) Laminar Research
   and the X-Plane Scenery Gateway contributors, released under the GNU General
   Public License.  Only derived stand-to-runway distances (`map_*` columns) are
   computed locally by `src/mapa.py`; no `apt.dat` content is redistributed here.
   <https://gateway.x-plane.com/> ·
   <https://developer.x-plane.com/article/airport-data-apt-dat-file-format-specification/>


